Library-level order: a library's rules come after every library it
depends on, even when alphabetical library-name order would put the
consumer first. `a_app` (alphabetically first) uses `Z_base.widget` from
library `z_base`, so `z_base`'s rules must come first.

  $ mkdir a_app z_base

  $ cat > z_base/z_base.ml <<EOF
  > [@@@css.config [("library", "z_base")]]
  > [@@@css ".base-widget{color:red;}"]
  > let widget () = ()
  > EOF

  $ cat > a_app/main.ml <<EOF
  > [@@@css.config [("library", "a_app")]]
  > [@@@css ".app-main{color:blue;}"]
  > let _ = Z_base.widget
  > EOF

  $ styled-ppx.generate a_app/main.ml z_base/z_base.ml
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  .base-widget{color:red;}
  .app-main{color:blue;}
